    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. Number of innovative models for selected sectoral municipal services designed and piloted in target municipalities
1.2. Number of citizen-driven monitoring mechanisms with direct feedback on provided services designed and piloted
1.3 Number of vulnerable/ marginalized group  representatives engaged in capacity development and co-design activities 
2.1. Number of youth-lead community initiatives in support to local democratization/development
2.2. Number of policy recommendations prepared by project-supported youth and ratio of consideration by the National Assembly
2.3. Number of solutions co-designed by multi-stakeholder groups for public services or participatory and cohesive governance
3.1 Share of the population in target municipalities that sees decision-making as inclusive and responsive.
3.2. Number of women running for/ being elected to local self-government. 
Percentage of women representation in community councils (Note: If proportional electoral system is introduced during 2021-2022 elections women representation will reach 30%)
3.4.  Number of target municipalities where women actively contribute to local decision-making (e.g. through participation in local decision-making processes and implementation of women-led initiatives)
3.5.  Number of target municipalities in which female local advisory committees are formed
3.6. Number of gender sensitive Annual Workplans developed based on the gender analysis data</narrative>
    </description>
